# Add project-specific packages for Buildroot here
#
# If these are non-proprietary, please consider contributing them back to
# Nerves or Buildroot.

# Sourced here, not nerves_system_sheng/Config.in: the Docker build_runner
# invokes create-build.sh from deps/nerves_system_br's own copy (mounted at
# /nerves/env/platform), whose own script-relative NERVES_SYSTEM/BR2_EXTERNAL
# resolution points at that shared platform tree - not this project's. Both
# trees register the same "NERVES" external name (see both external.desc
# files), so shared packages like boardid still resolve (from the platform's
# own copy), but packages that only exist here (ab_ops, ufs_boot_lun) never
# get sourced from nerves_system_sheng/Config.in at all - confirmed via the
# actual generated .config: boardid appeared as a real, recognized-but-
# disabled symbol, ab_ops/ufs_boot_lun didn't exist in it at all, not even
# as "not set". $NERVES_DEFCONFIG_DIR/Config.in (this file) is different -
# create-build.sh derives that path from the defconfig argument itself, not
# its own script location, so it reliably resolves to this board dir
# regardless of the platform-vs-project BR2_EXTERNAL ambiguity above.
# Not $BR2_EXTERNAL_NERVES_PATH: same ambiguity as above, so it'd point at
# the platform tree here too - use $NERVES_DEFCONFIG_DIR instead, proven
# reliable since it's literally how Kconfig found this very file.
source "$NERVES_DEFCONFIG_DIR/../../package/ab_ops/Config.in"
source "$NERVES_DEFCONFIG_DIR/../../package/ufs_boot_lun/Config.in"
